cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Chorus in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "Chorus: A unified interface for genomic sequence oracles"
type: software
version: 0.7.5
date-released: "2026-08-18"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/pinellolab/chorus"
abstract: >-
  Chorus provides one interface to eight genomic deep-learning oracles (Enformer,
  Borzoi, ChromBPNet/BPNet, Sei, LegNet, Cherimoya/CATv1, EPInformer-seq and
  AlphaGenome, the last with both a JAX and a PyTorch backend), each in its own
  isolated conda environment. Raw predictions are turned into percentiles against
  per-track empirical background nulls, so an effect size can be read across
  models and assays, and every analysis is reproducible from a code version paired
  with a dataset revision.
keywords:
  - genomics
  - deep-learning
  - regulatory-genomics
  - variant-effect-prediction
  - enformer
  - borzoi
  - chrombpnet
  - alphagenome
  - model-context-protocol
authors:
